{"from": "passage:mk-02-01", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-09-01", "note": "Both place the scene in Capernaum; Mark says 'after some days' and 'he was in the house', Matthew says he crossed by boat to 'his own city'."}
{"from": "passage:mk-02-03", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-09-02", "note": "A paralytic carried to Jesus on a mat/bed."}
{"from": "passage:mk-02-04", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-09-02", "note": "The paralytic let down before Jesus; Mark alone has the roof dug open."}
{"from": "passage:mk-02-05", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-09-02", "note": "'Son, your sins are forgiven you.'"}
{"from": "passage:mk-02-06", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-09-03", "note": "Scribes sitting there reason that claiming to forgive sins is blasphemy."}
{"from": "passage:mk-02-07", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-09-03", "note": "'Who can forgive sins but God alone?'"}
{"from": "passage:mk-02-10", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-09-06", "note": "'The Son of Man has authority on earth to forgive sins.'"}
{"from": "passage:mk-02-11", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-09-06", "note": "'Arise, take up your mat, and go to your house.'"}
{"from": "passage:mk-02-12", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-09-08", "note": "The paralytic rises and the crowds glorify God."}
{"from": "passage:mk-02-14", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-09-09", "note": "The same call of the tax collector at the tax office; Mark names Levi son of Alphaeus, Matthew names Matthew."}
{"from": "passage:mk-02-15", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-09-10", "note": "Many tax collectors and sinners recline at table with Jesus."}
{"from": "passage:mk-02-16", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-09-11", "note": "Scribes and Pharisees object that he eats with tax collectors and sinners."}
{"from": "passage:mk-02-18", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-09-14", "note": "John's disciples and the Pharisees are fasting and ask why Jesus' disciples do not."}
{"from": "passage:mk-02-19", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-09-15", "note": "The bridegroom saying: the groomsmen cannot fast while the bridegroom is with them."}
{"from": "passage:mk-02-21", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-09-16", "note": "No one sews unshrunk cloth on an old garment."}
{"from": "passage:mk-02-22", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-09-17", "note": "New wine into fresh wineskins, not old ones."}
{"from": "passage:mk-02-23", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-12-01", "note": "On the Sabbath through the grain fields the disciples pluck ears of grain."}
{"from": "passage:mk-02-24", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-12-02", "note": "The Pharisees call the plucking on the Sabbath unlawful."}
{"from": "passage:mk-02-25", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-12-03", "note": "'Have you not read what David did, when he had need, and was hungry?'"}
{"from": "passage:mk-02-26", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-12-04", "note": "David entered God's house and ate the showbread; Mark dates it 'in the days of Abiathar the high priest'."}
{"from": "claim:mk-02-04-roof-dug-through", "type": "mentions", "to": "person:jesus-of-nazareth"}
{"from": "claim:mk-02-04-roof-dug-through", "type": "mentions", "to": "place:capernaum"}
