{"from": "claim:mk-02-26-abiathar-high-priest", "type": "mentions", "to": "person:david"}
{"from": "site:capernaum-peter-house", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:mk-02-04-roof-dug-through", "grade": "C", "note": "The excavated 1st-century Capernaum dwelling shows the town's housing: coarse basalt-block walls, a courtyard with stairs leading to the roof, and (per the fetched Wikipedia article) a roof 'constructed of light wooden beams and thatch mixed with mud' - a roof that could be dug open. The excavation shows the construction custom, not this digging."}
{"from": "claim:mk-02-04-roof-dug-through", "type": "documented_by", "to": "source:wikipedia-capernaum-roof"}
{"from": "claim:mk-02-14-levi-alphaeus-tax-office", "type": "documented_by", "to": "source:wikipedia-matthew-levi"}
{"from": "claim:mk-02-14-levi-alphaeus-tax-office", "type": "documented_by", "to": "source:wikipedia-calling-matthew-telonion"}
{"from": "claim:mk-02-26-abiathar-high-priest", "type": "documented_by", "to": "source:wikipedia-abiathar-mark"}
{"from": "person:levi-son-of-alphaeus", "type": "documented_by", "to": "source:wikipedia-matthew-levi"}
{"from": "person:abiathar", "type": "documented_by", "to": "source:wikipedia-abiathar-mark"}
{"from": "claim:mk-02-04-roof-dug-through", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-09-02-paralytic-carried", "note": "Difference: Mark 2:4 records digging through the roof and lowering the mat; Matthew 9:2 simply has the paralytic brought to Jesus. The Wikipedia Capernaum article notes 'the narrative in Matthew 9:2-7 does not mention the paralytic being lowered through the roof'."}
{"from": "claim:mk-02-14-levi-alphaeus-tax-office", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-09-09-matthew-tax-office", "note": "Name difference: Mark 2:14 names the tax collector Levi son of Alphaeus; Matthew 9:9 names Matthew at the telonion. The fetched Wikipedia article states the parallel passages 'do not associate it with the name Matthew'."}
{"from": "person:levi-son-of-alphaeus", "type": "related_to", "to": "person:matthew-the-apostle", "note": "Traditional identification, not made by the texts: Mark 2:14 calls him Levi son of Alphaeus, Matthew 9:9 calls him Matthew; the fetched article says the passages 'do not associate it with the name Matthew'."}
{"from": "claim:mk-02-26-abiathar-high-priest", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-12-03-david-showbread", "note": "Priest-name difference: Mark 2:26 dates the showbread episode to 'Abiathar the high priest'; Matthew 12:4 follows 1 Samuel 21, where the priest at Nob is Ahimelech, Abiathar's father. The fetched Wikipedia article calls it 'a similar confusion', noting suggestions (double names, or Abiathar officiating in his father's stead) that 'have not been fully accepted'."}
{"from": "text:1-samuel-21-showbread", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mk-02-26-abiathar-high-priest", "note": "1 Samuel 21:1-6, the account Jesus cites, names Ahimelech son of Ahitub as the priest at Nob, not Abiathar. Biblical cross-reference, recorded as related_to."}
